[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536048628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112740#issuecomment-3536048628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112740","id":3536048628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sw9H0","user":{"login":"lodetrick","id":146759331,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL9eow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146759331?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick","html_url":"https://github.com/lodetrick","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lodetrick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-15T05:49:03Z","updated_at":"2025-11-15T05:53:19Z","body":"When working on #112792, I think I found a solution to this, it is to change the early exit condition in `_repaint` to:\r\n```c++\r\nbool panel_collapsed = get_current_tab() == -1;\r\nif (!panel_collapsed && (get_previous_tab() != -1)) {\r\n    return;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis way, repaint will now be called when both current_tab and previous_tab are -1, which will only be the case on startup. It appears that `_repaint` wasn't actually executing on startup due to this condition, even though we wanted it to be executed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3536048628/reactions","total_count":0